Method Returns <code>getLeaderboard(StatType, limit)</code> <code>CompletableFuture&lt;List&lt;LeaderboardEntry&gt;&gt;</code> (<code>getName()</code>, <code>getStats()</code>), best first, ties by name; <code>limit</code> 1 to 100 <code>loadStats(name)</code> <code>CompletableFuture&lt;Optional&lt;PlayerStatsView&gt;&gt;</code>, also for offline players; empty when the player never played <code>findPlayers(prefix, limit)</code> <code>CompletableFuture&lt;List&lt;String&gt;&gt;</code> names starting with <code>prefix</code> (case-insensitive) <code>loadStats(UUID)</code> (2.8-beta) like <code>loadStats(name)</code>, by UUID <code>addStat(UUID, name, StatType, amount)</code> (2.8-beta) adds <code>amount</code> (1 or more) to one stat and saves it like the stats of a game: <code>playerStats.json</code>, or MySQL (network-wide, in the leaderboards). Stats can't be lowered. Server thread only <p><code>StatType</code>: <code>WINS</code>, <code>LOSSES</code>, <code>KILLS</code>, <code>DEATHS</code>, <code>FINAL_KILLS</code>, <code>BEDS_BROKEN</code>, <code>GAMES_PLAYED</code> (<code>stat.of(view)</code> reads the value). With JSON storage the data comes from memory (the future completes on the server thread); with MySQL storage the database is asked on its own thread, so the results cover the whole network. Call them from any thread and never block the server thread on the future.</p> <pre><code>api.getLeaderboard(StatType.WINS, 10).thenAccept(top -&gt;
        top.forEach(e -&gt; getLogger().info(e.getName() + ": " + e.getStats().getWins())));

// an addon game mode counts its own wins (2.8-beta)
api.addStat(winner.getUniqueId(), winner.getName(), StatType.WINS, 1);
</code></pre> <p><code>addStat</code> changes only the stat you pass; a win doesn't add a game played, so add <code>GAMES_PLAYED</code> yourself when it should count as a game.</p>
